## Historical v9 chapter acceptance details

### Chapter 0 — Executive summary

- Identify the target first.
- State cutoff and scope.
- Reconcile headline counts.
- Identify verified developments.
- Identify unresolved leads.
- State immediate actions.
- State the legal boundary.

### Chapter 1 — Overview

- Show target and comparison parties.
- Show alias coverage.
- Show target roles.
- Separate candidate and verified patents.
- Separate family members and families.
- Separate proceedings and events.
- Explain review caps.

### Chapter 2 — Family basics

- State family definition.
- Show asserted member.
- Show related members.
- Show member-specific status.
- Show as-of dates.
- Show representative claims.
- Show translation provenance.
- Show geographic limits.

### Chapter 3 — Timeline

- Use chronological order.
- Include case ID.
- Include relevant patent number.
- Include event type.
- Include target role.
- Include primary source.
- Include evidence state.
- Preserve uncertain dates.

### Chapter 4 — Patent details

- Use publication number as visible identifier.
- Link only to a safe stable destination.
- Show title and status date.
- Show target role and linked cases.
- Show asserted claims only when verified.
- Show technical problem, means, and effect.
- Show image only when safe.
- Show family table.
- Show sources and open questions.

### Chapter 5 — Case deep dives

- Use official caption and number.
- Identify tribunal and jurisdiction.
- Identify all material parties.
- Label allegations.
- Label defenses.
- Describe procedural posture.
- Distinguish orders and holdings.
- Describe disposition accurately.
- Describe appeal status.
- Provide monitoring triggers.

### Chapter 6 — Inventors

- State identity method.
- State lookback.
- State counting rule.
- Show yearly counts.
- Show classifications.
- Show technology themes.
- Show representative patents.
- State descriptive limitation.

### Chapter 7 — Conclusions

- Cite geographic evidence.
- Cite case posture.
- Cite patent and claim evidence.
- Cite inventor evidence.
- Separate fact and inference.
- State uncertainty.
- Provide trigger and action.
- Avoid outcome prediction.

### Chapter 8 — Summary list

- Reconcile every case.
- Reconcile every asserted patent.
- Reconcile every family member.
- Reconcile every target role.
- Reconcile every evidence state.
- Reconcile every source ID.
- State cutoff and family rule.

## Historical v9 presentation tokens

Use these semantic roles rather than copying the source's decorative values:

- `paper`: white report surface.
- `canvas`: cool neutral page background.
- `ink`: high-contrast charcoal text.
- `muted`: secondary slate text.
- `navy`: primary heading and navigation accent.
- `blue`: link and evidence accent.
- `line`: neutral table and card border.
- `panel`: subtle metadata background.
- `elevated`: muted red text plus explicit label.
- `moderate`: muted amber text plus explicit label.
- `lower_on_reviewed_evidence`: muted green text plus explicit label.
- `not_assessable`: neutral gray text plus explicit label.

Use responsive one-column cards on narrow screens, scroll wrappers for wide tables, visible keyboard focus, semantic buttons only when interaction is necessary, and complete print rendering without hidden substantive content.
